  "response": "Based on the provided vulnerability description, I will assess the CVSS v3.1 base metric.\n\n**Attack Vector (AV)**: The issue is an input validation issue in the Harbor registry integration, which could allow a maintainer to add malicious code to the CLI commands shown in the UI. This suggests that the attack vector is **Network (N)**.\n\n**Attack Complexity (AC)**: The vulnerability requires some level of expertise and knowledge of the Harbor registry integration to exploit. Therefore, I assess the attack complexity as **Low (L)**.\n\n**Privileges Required (PR)**: To exploit this vulnerability, an attacker would need to have maintainer privileges or higher. Therefore, I assess the privileges required as **High (H)**.\n\n**User Interaction (UI)**: The vulnerability can be exploited without user interaction, as it is an input validation issue that can be triggered programmatically. Therefore, I assess the user interaction as **No (N)**.\n\n**Scope (S)**: The scope of this vulnerability is **Unchanged (U)**, as it affects all versions of Product Y EE starting from 14.9 before 17.8.6, all versions starting from 17.9 before 17.8.3, and all versions starting from 17.10 before 17.10.1.\n\n**Confidentiality Impact (C)**: The vulnerability could allow an attacker to add malicious code to the CLI commands shown in the UI, which could potentially lead to confidentiality breaches. Therefore, I assess the confidentiality impact as **High (H)**.\n\n**Integrity Impact (I)**: The vulnerability could also allow an attacker to modify or delete data stored in the Harbor registry integration, which could potentially lead to integrity breaches. Therefore, I assess the integrity impact as **High (H)**.\n\n**Availability Impact (A)**: The vulnerability could potentially cause a denial-of-service (DoS) or a crash of the affected system, leading to availability impacts. Therefore, I assess the availability impact as **High (H)**.\n\nHere is the output in JSON format:\n\n```